The previous version trapped because it called `expect` and `assert!` when the store had no `urls` entry or the list came out empty. This version never traps. It tries a few likely keys (`urls`, `subscriptions`, `feeds`) and parses the value as newline-, comma- or whitespace-separated URLs, or as a JSON-style array. If the store has nothing, it returns an empty list. I haven't compiled or run it.

